  "expected_answer": "The web project's Framework Preset on Vercel is \"other\" (the deploy log in revert.reason says `Framework Preset: other`), so the build was treated as a static site looking for a public/ folder. Fix: set the project's Framework Preset to Next.js (Vercel: Project Settings -> Build and Deployment), then redeploy once the operator says yes.",
  "final_text": "Vercel treated `gamma-research` as a **static site**. Its project settings show `Framework Preset: other`, so after `npm run build` succeeded, Vercel looked for a `public` output directory. This app is a Next.js app: it has an `app/` directory and runs `next build`, which produces `.next` output rather than a `public` build directory. The app’s [`vercel.json`](/tmp/sf-bench-t4_diagnose_deploy-cjl7drrb/factory/build/gamma_app/vercel.json) doesn’t set an output directory.\n\nThe fix is to change the Vercel project’s **Framework Preset** to **Next.js**, leaving the Output Directory at its Next.js default, then redeploy. The error points to a Vercel project setting mismatch; adding a `public` directory would mask it rather than configure this Next.js app correctly.",
